service - The Legacy Wrapper
Basic Syntax : sudo service SERVICE_NAME COMMAND
Commands
sudo service nginx start      # Start service
sudo service nginx stop       # Stop service
sudo service nginx restart    # Restart service
sudo service nginx status     # Check status
sudo service nginx reload     # Reload configuration

How service Works
The service command is a wrapper that:
- Checks if systemd is available → uses systemctl
- Falls back to SysV init scripts in /etc/init.d/
- Handles the translation automatically


