## System Configuration

### Journal Settings (`/etc/systemd/journald.conf`)

```ini
# Size limits
SystemMaxUse=1G              # Max total disk usage
SystemMaxFileSize=100M       # Max per file
SystemMaxFiles=100           # Max number of files

# Retention
MaxRetentionSec=1month       # Max age of logs

# Forwarding to syslog (if needed)
ForwardToSyslog=no
ForwardToWall=yes

# Compression
Compress=yes

# Log Level
MaxLevelStore=debug          # Store up to debug level
MaxLevelSyslog=debug         # Forward up to debug level
```

**Apply changes:**
```bash
sudo systemctl restart systemd-journald
```

### Persistent vs Volatile Storage

```bash
# Check if persistent storage is enabled
ls -la /var/log/journal/

# Enable persistent storage
sudo mkdir -p /var/log/journal
sudo systemd-tmpfiles --create --prefix /var/log/journal

# Force flush logs to disk
sudo journalctl --flush
```

